                <pb facs="0333" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg227"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-11-11"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11, 1891</hi>.</date>
                        (Received December 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 229.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The two houses of the national Congress met
                    in session on yesterday and proceeded to organize. The three gentlemen composing
                    the Junta de Gobierno, or Provisional Government, resigned; one of them, Señor
                    Don Waldo Silva, was elected president of the Senate; the second, Señor Don
                    Barros Luco, president of the Chamber of Deputies; and Señor Don Jorge Montt,
                    who has been unanimously nominated for the Presidency, was temporarily invested
                    by Congress with fall presidential powers, pending the regular election by
                    presidential voters and his regular installation. The Chamber then proceeded to
                    elect various officers and its quota of the council of state, and as all were
                    elected from among what is known as the Liberal alliance, the Conservative
                    members of the cabinet resigned, namely, the minister of interior and the
                    secretary of the treasury, and up to the time of writing their successors have
                    not been selected.</p>
                <p>Under the new and regular Government I look for a more liberal policy, more
                    leniency toward the vanquished partisans of the late Government, and a kindlier
                    feeling toward the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Patrick Egan</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
